# Allowlist for scripts/ci-guards/pre/no-instant-now.sh (work-plan rule R6).
#
# One line per file: path|max|category|owner|reason
#   max       the most zero-argument Instant.now() calls the file may keep. It only goes down:
#             run  bash scripts/ci-guards/pre/no-instant-now.sh --tighten  after removing calls.
#   category  (file level: the strictest call in the file decides)
#             business    a call decides a business field (event time, last read, source
#                         modified time, age evaluation): an R6 violation to remove.
#             processing  an audit stamp, a response timestamp, a checkpoint or a dashboard
#                         window: the time the service acted. Tolerated until the module owns a
#                         Clock bean, then replaced with Instant.now(clock).
#   owner     the work package expected to clear the entry, or - when none is assigned.
#   reason    what the call does.
# Sorted by path. Adding a file here, or raising a number, is not allowed.
